                <pb facs="0425" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg421"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.112/19: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-29T18:00:00+08:00">July 29, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 29—8:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>385. Department’s 221, July 28, 7 p.m.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d567-f1"/> and
                    Chefoo’s July 28, 11 a.m. I have sent the following instructions to Chefoo:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“July 29, 6 p.m. Your July 27, 9 p.m. and July 28, 11 a.m. You are
                            authorized to accept expression of regret as conveyed to you and
                            consider incident closed. I am glad to observe that you are able to
                            settle these matters locally.</p>
                        <p>Sent to Chefoo, repeated to Peiping and Shanghai, Peiping please repeat
                            to Tokyo.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I am separately instructing Peiping and Chefoo along the lines of Department’s
                    220, July 28, 6 p.m.<anchor n="37" xml:id="d567-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
